      "text_helper": "Section 22.7.2 \"Command completion signal enable\" in chapter 22 (Secure digital input/output interface (SDIO)), RM0008 Rev 21, page 606.",
      "section_content": "If the ‘enable CMD completion’ bit SDIO_CMD[12] is set and the ‘not interrupt Enable’ bit\nSDIO_CMD[13] is set, the CPSM waits for the command completion signal in the Waitcpl\nstate.\nWhen ‘0’ is received on the CMD line, the CPSM enters the Idle state. No new command\ncan be sent for 7 bit cycles. Then, for the last 5 cycles (out of the 7) the CMD line is driven to\n‘1’ in push-pull mode.",
